{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787186107357095002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"glacial-gleaming-ray","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"cd315547bc039eb2ad9f58e316caf6ff56f5a75f3687553a678237458c51d995","event_uuid":"61249a1f-d682-466f-a1d6-8607ebaf31a5","position":{"commit_sha":"601b9daab18a7030e77f50b7866f418e53ba31eb","position":"1787185959426553001-61249a1f-d682-466f-a1d6-8607ebaf31a5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0879f8e2e8df7ad094f48344b4aa3d907500f195a92a302030f792cb6476ad44","event_uuid":"284cd4bc-7f36-47c8-b78a-8cca0fac9d0e","position":{"commit_sha":"26084a7840cdedc2b4b1f2413f9d4ac7ba6526a5","position":"1787186037764797001-284cd4bc-7f36-47c8-b78a-8cca0fac9d0e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ed64e44d2bc262e22c438556cbe71c5fb9e21a5accadbfa0e79cc5aefa7252c8","event_uuid":"3203dae8-41d5-485f-85c9-3995e5cb7989","position":{"commit_sha":"fab41d511287c2f71872455a287a7d06e7ffc98e","position":"1787186107357095001-3203dae8-41d5-485f-85c9-3995e5cb7989"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787185959426553001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"284cd4bc-7f36-47c8-b78a-8cca0fac9d0e","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"3726-a1b0-c9bb-4d83"}],"description":"## What\n\nParametrize the existing detector and close-guard suites over both `[non-codebase]` and\n`[operator-attested]` so the alias has an explicit regression suite rather than relying on the\nold tests incidentally still passing.\n\n## Scope\n\nAdd a both-spellings case to: `tests/unit/test_det_attestation_launder.py`,\n`tests/unit/test_det_measurement_provenance{,_heldout}.py`,\n`tests/unit/test_attested_close_guard.py`,\n`tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_attested_close_guard_e2e.py`,\n`tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_ac_checkbox_precheck{,_heldout}.py`,\n`tests/unit/test_a8e5_operator_attested_edge.py`.\n\nDecide and pin the near-miss policy for the new tag: `[operator_attested]` is a DELIBERATE\nnon-match asserted in ~15 places (ADR-0043). `[non_codebase]` and `[noncodebase]` need the\nsame treatment.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Each listed suite exercises both spellings and asserts identical outcomes.\n- [ ] `[non_codebase]` and `[noncodebase]` are asserted NOT to match, mirroring the existing\n      `[operator_attested]` contract.\n- [ ] No existing assertion was weakened to make the new cases pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_det_attestation_launder.py","reason":"parametrize over both spellings"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_det_measurement_provenance.py","reason":"parametrize over both spellings"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_ac_checkbox_precheck.py","reason":"parametrize over both spellings"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_a8e5_operator_attested_edge.py","reason":"near-miss policy for the new tag"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","3726-a1b0-c9bb-4d83"],["parent","6f5a-4a49-7bbf-4a30"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"6f5a-4a49-7bbf-4a30","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"a859-4d8b-c558-463d","ticket_type":"story","title":"S3 — compatibility regression suite: both spellings behave identically","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["61249a1f-d682-466f-a1d6-8607ebaf31a5","284cd4bc-7f36-47c8-b78a-8cca0fac9d0e","3203dae8-41d5-485f-85c9-3995e5cb7989"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787186107357095002,"uuid":"d5fe7f57-759e-4491-89d6-d0adc8400e2d"}